# Monitor static bundle: feature matrix vs `--disable-*`

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

- **Canonical build**: **`HPCPerfStats/monitor/scripts/build_static_bundle.sh`** probes the host and may pass **`--disable-infiniband`**, **`--disable-gpu`**, **`--disable-amd-gpu`**, etc., when matching devel stacks are missing. See **monitor-static-build-verification** for verification steps.
- **Infiniband**:
  - Disabling **does not always mean “no IB counters.”** Some paths use **sysfs** (`/sys/class/infiniband`) without libibverbs/MAD; others require **MAD** / full verbs stack.
  - When changing IB-related code, state clearly whether the change affects **sysfs-only**, **MAD**, or **both**, and whether **`--disable-infiniband`** is expected to remove all IB-related output.
  - **Fleet / dlopen:** **`--enable-ib-mad-dlopen`** compiles MAD against vendored `third_party/ibmad-shim/` and loads `libibmad` at runtime — **no** `-libmad` in `NEEDED`, **no** BuildRequires on InfiniBand devel for fleet RPMs.
- **Omni-Path**:
  - Sysfs `host_opa` is always built. Link-time **`--enable-opa`** needs IFS/`liboib_utils` on the build host.
  - **Fleet:** **`--enable-opa-mad-dlopen`** uses vendored `third_party/oib-shim/` + runtime `dlopen` of `liboib_utils` (`HPCPERFSTATS_OIB_LIB`). Do **not** document dual IB+OPA BuildRequires as the Stampede3 fleet path. Lonestar6 fleet does **not** enable OPA MAD.
- **Stampede3 one-build RPM**:
  - Entrypoint: **`scripts/prepare_rpmbuild_stampede3.sh`** → calls **`prepare_rpmbuild_dirs.sh`** and prints the **same** `rpmbuild -ba` footer (no alternate `_topdir` / second spec).
  - Fleet signal (opt-in only): **`HPCS_BUNDLE_FLEET=stampede3`** and/or **`scripts/fleet/stampede3.force`** created by **`prepare_rpmbuild_stampede3.sh`** and embedded by **`dist-hook`** when present. Default **`prepare_rpmbuild_dirs.sh`** must **not** ship or require the force file (never commit it).
  - Matrix: `--enable-ib-mad-dlopen`, `--enable-opa-mad-dlopen`, `--disable-amd-gpu`, `--enable-intel-gpu` when XPUM headers are vendored; never auto `--disable-infiniband` solely for missing build-host PCI/devel.
  - **intel-gpu on aarch64:** static bundle does **not** auto `--enable-intel-gpu` from vendored XPUM alone; requires fleet, or **`HPCS_BUNDLE_ENABLE_INTEL_GPU=1`**. x86 keeps vendored-header auto-enable.
- **Lonestar6 one-build RPM**:
  - Entrypoint: **`scripts/prepare_rpmbuild_ls6.sh`** → same **`prepare_rpmbuild_dirs.sh`** footer pattern as Stampede3.
  - Fleet signal (opt-in only): **`HPCS_BUNDLE_FLEET=ls6`** and/or **`scripts/fleet/ls6.force`** (created by prepare; embedded by **`dist-hook`**; never commit). Explicit **`HPCS_BUNDLE_FLEET`** wins if multiple fleet markers exist.
  - Matrix: `--enable-ib-mad-dlopen`, `--disable-amd-gpu`, **`--disable-intel-gpu`** (forced even when vendored XPUM headers exist on x86); **do not** `--enable-opa-mad-dlopen`; never auto `--disable-infiniband`. NVIDIA stays on default x86 DCGM runtime-dlopen (covers `a100`; idle on CPU-only `genoa`/`milan`).
- **Horizon one-build RPM** (first shared-node fleet):
  - Entrypoint: **`scripts/prepare_rpmbuild_horizon.sh`** → same **`prepare_rpmbuild_dirs.sh`** footer pattern.
  - Fleet signal (opt-in only): **`HPCS_BUNDLE_FLEET=horizon`** and/or **`scripts/fleet/horizon.force`** (created by prepare; embedded by **`dist-hook`**; never commit).
  - Matrix: **`--enable-shared-node-multi-jid`**, `--enable-ib-mad-dlopen`, `--disable-amd-gpu`, **`--disable-intel-gpu`**; **do not** `--enable-opa-mad-dlopen`; never auto `--disable-infiniband`. Deploy consumer (listend) before Horizon shared-node monitor RPMs.
- **GPU paths**: NVIDIA vs AMD have separate disable flags; **`--disable-gpu`** vs vendor-specific options must stay consistent with **`configure.ac`** and **`build_static_bundle.sh`**.
- **CPU counters / LIKWID**: x86 uses exclusive LIKWID; aarch64 `auto` uses the `arm` backend (`/proc/stat` util, cpufreq clock, direct perf core + Grace SCF counters; no DCGM, **no LIKWID** since 3.1). `host_power_socket` (hwmon) builds on every arch. **GPU:** `nvidia_gpu` is always built with runtime `dlopen` (DCGM + NVML) on every arch; the bundle passes `--disable-gpu` only when vendored DCGM headers are missing. Bundle, prepare and cross build LIKWID static archives on **x86 only**. See **monitor-dcgm-integration** and **monitor-arm-direct-perf** when touching `cpu_counter_metrics*` / `arm_*perf*`.
- **Docs**: If behavior changes, update **`README.md`** or packaging notes per **monitor-readme-maintenance** when user-visible flags or outputs change.
